## Lexical/NLP Feature Options for Group Interaction Transcripts

### 1. **Classical Text Features**
| Feature | Description | Use Case |
|---------|-------------|----------|
| **TF-IDF** | Term importance weighted by rarity | Topic differentiation across tasks |
| **POS distributions** | % nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns | Cognitive load, formality |
| **Readability** | Flesch-Kincaid, SMOG grade | Complexity of explanations |
| **Dependency depth** | Parse tree complexity | Syntactic sophistication |

### 2. **Psycholinguistic Dictionaries**
| Tool | What it measures |
|------|------------------|
| **LIWC** | 90+ categories (cognitive, social, affective) |
| **NRC Emotion Lexicon** | 8 emotions + valence |
| **Affective Norms (VAD)** | Valence, arousal, dominance per word |
| **MRC Database** | Concreteness, imageability, familiarity |

### 3. **Dialogue/Discourse Analysis**
- **Dialogue act classification** (question, statement, backchannel, suggestion)
- **Topic modeling** (LDA/BERTopic) — track topic shifts within tasks
- **Discourse markers** ("so", "well", "I mean") — cognitive processing signals
- **Argumentation mining** — claim/premise detection

### 4. **Transformer-Based (Big Models)**
| Approach | Model | Output |
|----------|-------|--------|
| **Sentence embeddings** | Sentence-BERT | 768-dim vectors per utterance |
| **Emotion classification** | GoEmotions (27 emotions) | Fine-grained emotion per turn |
| **Personality from text** | BERT fine-tuned on Big Five | Estimated personality traits |
| **Dialogue act** | DialoGPT / ConvBERT | Intent classification |
| **Semantic similarity** | all-MiniLM-L6-v2 | Between-speaker alignment |
| **Summarization** | BART/T5 | Task-level summaries |
| **Zero-shot classification** | BART-MNLI | Any label without training |

### 5. **Group Dynamics Features** (Most Relevant)
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Lexical accommodation** | Do speakers mirror each other's words? |
| **Semantic alignment** | Embedding similarity between consecutive turns |
| **Information novelty** | New concepts introduced per speaker |
| **Dominance markers** | "I think" vs "We should" |
| **Inclusive language** | We/our vs I/my ratio |

